  <notes>
    <note date="2026-10-08">FROM T218e: the "Secure Record Owner" role is NOT in SpaarkeMaster and cannot be — Dataverse packages no role authored in a child business unit ("Subcomponent ... cannot be added to the solution because the root component Role is missing"), and UAC-r2 contains it in the Secure Record unit on purpose (SECURE-PROJECT-ENVIRONMENT-SETUP.md 5.2). So H7b MUST create it: in the Secure Record unit, with exactly the Read-at-Basic privileges of config/secure-record-owner-role.json (the same file and checks as scripts/Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1: metadata privilege names, read back, never wider), then assign it to the named owner team. Coordination note: notes/coordination/2026-10-08-to-uac-r2-2.md.</note>
    <note date="2026-10-08">DONE (worktree agent, FULL rigor; no live action). H7b built: Handlers/SecureRecordSetup/ (handler, SecureRecordSetupProcedure, ISecureRecordSetupDataverse + DataverseWebApiSecureRecordSetup, SecureRecordOwnerRoleSet = L2 reader of the linked config/secure-record-owner-role.json, SecureRecordSetupIntake, rejection codes, module). Five-place registration (HandlerIds + Dispatchable = 21, keyed forwarder, SecureRecordSetupModule + one Program.cs line, DAG). DAG: [H7b]={H6}; H9 += H7b (no BFF deploy without sprk_noaccessentry / NULL-flag repair / secure anchor); H13 += H7b. Steps: P0 sprk_noaccessentry probe with the BFF reader's $select; S0; root unit; S4 root-role check (a root "Secure Record Owner" would replicate everywhere — T218e); S5 metadata names; S1 + T2 (direct child of root, else quarantine); S2; S3; S4 (replica refused); S5 depth; S10 profiles (shipped — verified, never created); S12 writer-profile membership lock; S14 sprk_issecure lock (shipped — verified); T4 root default team; then writes: S1 unit, S3 team, S4 role IN the unit, S5 add, S6 strip ALWAYS, S7, S8 (role off default team; System Administrator off both), S11 reader profile to every default team, S12 H10's two app users, S13 NULL flags; S9 verify. Every refusal precedes the first write. Dry run = intake secureRecordSetupDryRun ("true"/"false", validated at POST /api/runs with the handler's code secure_setup.dry_run_invalid): reads everything, zero writes, plan in gate h7b-secure-setup-plan, run stops (Resumable secure_setup.dry_run). Auth: the BFF app registration via EnvVarValuesOptions + WorkerDataverseCredentialFactory (H7's identity and options — no new setting or secret). Owner-team name = BFF compiled default; unit/role names from the file; no run parameters for them (manifest sets no SecureRecord__ key — pinned). Tests: L2 2442 (+90 H7b), ArchTests 855 (+14 SecureRecordOwnerRoleSetParityTests: both readers on the live file and the same bad documents; team/unit names; RowSelect parity; manifest). NOT built (owner decision, ISS-010 (#1486)): INCOMING-145 §6 T1/T3/T5 — customer unit, BFF app users and guests in it; consequence found: H11 puts guests in the ROOT unit with Spaarke Basic User (Deep read on project/matter/work assignment) so every guest reads every secure record by depth, and H13 does not run the isolation census. Open with UAC-r2: #1364 confirmation (ISS-001 updated — the repo answers all four questions) and INCOMING-145 §4 item 1 (cascade-Assign probe with SharePoint locations). Live verification: T186.</note>
